# Push and local storage

## FCM

- `firebaseMessagingBackgroundHandler` stays top-level with `@pragma('vm:entry-point')`. The background isolate may call `Firebase.initializeApp` and `DatabaseService` only.
- Persist through `_persistRemoteMessage`, then increment `messageListRevision`. `HomeScreen` listens to that notifier. Do not add a second refresh channel.
- Title and body: `notification` fields, then `data['title']` / `data['body']`, then `'Notification'` / `''`.
- Foreground local notification: always on Android. On iOS only when `message.notification == null`, because iOS already presents notification payloads.
- Android channel id is `notif_app_channel`. Keep it equal to `com.google.firebase.messaging.default_notification_channel_id` in `android/app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml`.
- `syncToken` returns immediately unless a user and a non-empty base URL are saved. `device_id` is at most 50 characters.

## sqflite

Database file `notif_app.db`, version `_dbVersion` (currently 1). Tables: `settings`, `user`, `messages`.

There is no `onUpgrade`. A schema change bumps `_dbVersion` and adds `onUpgrade` that alters existing installs. Do not put the new columns only in `onCreate`.

`insertMessage` removes `id` so SQLite assigns it.
